 "verdict": "RUNG (class stability across two census seeds, as 17/17 base models achieved): 6 of 6 instruct models keep their class. Stable, so a class difference below is a difference and not resolution. PRIMARY (the clean pairs): Llama-3.2-3B [none] -> Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct [none]  unchanged; stablelm-3b-4e1t [none] -> stablelm-zephyr-3b [none]  unchanged. The fixed-point class SURVIVES instruction tuning on the clean pairs: the geometry is set in pretraining and behavioural tuning does not move it. That extends 'recipe shapes the geometry' rather than contradicting it \u2014 the recipes that move the class are the ones that change pretraining, not the ones that change behaviour. CONTEXT (loose pairs \u2014 generation or size is confounded with tuning in every one, so these are direction only): SmolLM-1.7B [funnel] -> SmolLM2-1.7B-Instruct [funnel]; gemma-2-2b [fragmented] -> gemma-1.1-2b-it [funnel]; Qwen1.5-1.8B [funnel] -> Qwen2.5-3B-Instruct [none]; Falcon3-1B-Base [borderline] -> Falcon3-3B-Instruct [funnel]. PRIOR-ART GATE OWED: the measurement above stands, but 'instruction tuning changes fixed-point structure' is a novelty claim against a literature this project has not searched \u2014 instruction-tuning-and-degeneration, which is not the distillation/pruning literature already checked. No novelty claim until F90/F91's check runs. BOUNDARY: 6 pairs, 2 of them clean; the rest confound generation or size with tuning. 96 starts, two census seeds, one greedy map per model. The class is a coarse four-way label and a within-class shift would not show here.",
 "_analysis_provenance": {
  "script": "argmax_census_instruct.py",
